ParentVault_closeEpoch
├── when caller does not have EPOCH_OPERATOR_ROLE
│   └── it should revert
├── when rebalance is in progress
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__RebalanceInProgress
├── when epoch is not open
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__EpochNotOpen
├── when epoch period is too short
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__EpochTooShort
├── when epoch has no deposits and no withdrawals
│   └── it should revert with ParentVault__EmptyEpoch
├── it should store pricePerShare on the epoch
├── it should store totalWithdrawClaimAmount on the epoch
├── it should store closedAtTimestamp on the epoch
├── it should update totalShares
├── it should make the epoch claimable
├── it should open the next epoch
├── when fee would consume TVL
│   └── it should skip fee and leave high water mark unchanged
├── when local strategy has net deposit
│   ├── it should deposit net flow into the adapter
│   ├── it should emit EpochClaimable
│   └── it should emit DepositToStrategySuccess
├── when local strategy has net withdrawal
│   ├── it should withdraw net flow from the adapter
│   ├── it should update totalWithdrawClaimAmount when adapter returns a different amount
│   ├── it should emit EpochClaimable
│   └── it should emit WithdrawFromStrategySuccess
├── when remote strategy has net deposit
│   ├── it should bridge net flow to the strategy chain
│   └── it should emit EpochClaimable
├── when remote strategy has net withdrawal
│   ├── it should mark the epoch executing
│   └── it should emit EpochExecuting
└── when local adapter reverts
    ├── it should revert on net deposit
    └── it should revert on net withdrawal
